    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Unfortunately I don&#39;t believe log_mix is vectorized. But you can vectorize the beta_binomial that you use later in your model. Instead of<div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">J</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> increment_log_prob</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> beta_binomial_log</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">Y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\">R</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\">alpha</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> gene_index</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\">beta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> gene_index</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">])</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br><br></span></div></code></div><br></div><div>you can do something like</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"color:#000\">model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real alphas</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">J</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real betas</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">J</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">// ... other stuff in model block</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">j </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">J</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    alphas</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">j</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> alpha</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">gene_index</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">j</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    betas</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">j</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> beta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">gene_index</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">j</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  increment_log_prob</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">beta_binomial_log</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">Y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> R</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> alphas</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> betas</span><span style=\"color:#660\">));</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// or Y ~ beta_binomial(R, alpha, beta)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span></font></div></code></div><br></div><div>which should be faster than putting the beta_binomial_log within the loop. </div><div><br></div><div>Jonah</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
